        "original_id": "b31bc3b9-04b7-5006-943e-c298a8f39be9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Caldera de Taburiente National Park, Teide National Park, La Palma, Tenerife, Canary Islands, Spain\n- Products/Systems: Echium wildpretii subsp. trichosiphon, Adenocarpus viscosus\n- Organizations: Corona Forestal Nature Park, Reserva Especial de las Palomas\n\nFacts:\n- Caldera de Taburiente National Park is a large geological feature on the island of La Palma in the Canary Islands of Spain.\n- Teide National Park is a national park located in Tenerife in the Canary Islands of Spain.\n- Adenocarpus viscosus can be found above 1800 meters on La Palma in Caldera de Taburiente.\n- Adenocarpus viscosus can be found above 1800 meters on Tenerife, where it is a dominant shrub in Teide National Park.\n- Adenocarpus viscosus also occurs in parts of Corona Forestal Nature Park and Reserva Especial de las Palomas on Tenerife.",
